$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The Schlenk technique was used. N-Bocprotected L-4-iodophenylalanine
methyl ester (849 mg, 2.10 x 10-3 mol) was dissolved in a solution of
3,4-dimethyl-2-phenyl-1-tributylstannylphosphole (10.5 mL, 0.2 M, 2.10 x
10-3 mol) in THF.Pd(dba)2 (24 mg, 4.19 x 10-5 mol, 2 mol%) was added and
the reaction mixture was stirred for 12 h at 60 °C. After cooling off the
reaction mixture to r.t., an aliquot was taken (conversion: 100%).
Product.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Stille cross-coupling
