$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Stille Coupling Reaction Catalyzed by
Water-Soluble Palladacyclic Aqua Complexes in Water. The Stille coupling
reaction of 3-I-C6H4CO2H (294 μmol) with PhSnCl3 (294 μmol) also proceeds
efficiently using [4]+ as a catalyst (0.002 mol %) in water at pH 10.5 at
100 °C (eq 5). As shown in Table 6, the yield of the product
(3-Ph-C6H4CO2H) was 100% for 12 h with a high TON of 50 000. Thus, the
catalyst [4]+ can also be used as an effective catalyst for the Stille
coupling reaction in water for practical use. (3-Ph-C6H4CO2H), Yiel 100%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM pH-Dependent C-C Coupling Reactions Catalyzed by Water-Soluble
Palladacyclic Aqua Catalysts in Water
