$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
3-(Fur-2-yl)-5-(thien-2-yl)-4H-1,2,6-thiadiazin-4-one (12a). To a stirred
solution of 3-chloro-5-(thien-2-yl)-4H-1,2,6-thiadiazin-4-one (11a) (50.0
mg, 0.22 mmol) in MeCN (2 mL) at rt, was added 2-(tributylstannyl)furan
(83 μL, 0.264 mmol) and Pd(Ph3P)2Cl2 (7.7 mg, 0.011 mmol) and the mixture
was heated at reflux until no starting material remained (TLC). The
reaction mixture was then allowed to cool to rt, diluted (DCM) and
adsorbed onto silica. Chromatography (hexane/DCM, 7:3) gave the title
compound 12a.
3-(1-Methyl-1H-pyrrol-2-yl)-5-(thien-2-yl)-4H-1,2,6-thiadiazin-4-one
(12b), yield 100%. mp 114.5-115.5 °C (from cyclohexane), Rf 0.31
(hexane/DCM, 7:3); (found: C, 52.3; H, 3.2; N, 15.4. C12H9N3OS2 requires
C, 52.3; H, 3.3; N, 15.3%); max(DCM)/nm 260 (log å 3.82), 344 inf (3.62),
378 (3.97), 381 (3.98), 420 inf (3.89), 432 (3.91); νmax/cm-1 3152w and
3059w (Ar CH), 2997w, 2945w, 1647w, 1614s (C=O), 1524w, 1506w, 1489m,
1464w, 1447w, 1410m, 1422m, 1373m, 1366m, 1296m, 1269w, 1242w, 1217w,
1136w, 1096w, 1067m, 1049m, 1034w, 978w, 895w, 872m, 856w, 845w, 837w,
822w; H(500 MHz; CDCl3) 8.19 (1H, d, J 4.0, thienyl H), 7.77 (1H, dd, J
4.0, 1.5, pyrrolyl H), 7.59 (1H, d, J 5.0, thienyl H), 7.17 (1H, dd, J
4.3, 4.3, thienyl H), 6.87 (1H, br s, pyrrolyl H), 6.24 (1H, dd, J 3.8,
2.8, pyrrolyl H), 3.97 (3H, s, NCH3); C(125 MHz; CDCl3) 161.9 (s), 153.2
(s), 152.4 (s), 136.8 (s), 132.4 (d), 131.2 (d), 131.0 (d), 127.5 (d),
126.5 (s), 120.5 (d), 108.5 (d), 38.6 (NCH3); m/z (EI) 275 (M+, 95%), 141
(100), 138 (64), 109 (21), 106 (30), 97 (7), 78 (8), 64 (5), 58 (6).
