$DATUM 75-05-8
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
3-(Fur-2-yl)-5-(thien-2-yl)-4H-1,2,6-thiadiazin-4-one (12a). To a stirred
solution of 3-chloro-5-(thien-2-yl)-4H-1,2,6-thiadiazin-4-one (11a) (50.0
mg, 0.22 mmol) in MeCN (2 mL) at rt, was added 2-(tributylstannyl)furan
(83 μL, 0.264 mmol) and Pd(Ph3P)2Cl2 (7.7 mg, 0.011 mmol) and the mixture
was heated at reflux until no starting material remained (TLC). The
reaction mixture was then allowed to cool to rt, diluted (DCM) and
adsorbed onto silica. Chromatography (hexane/DCM, 7:3) gave the title
compound 12a.
3-(Fur-2-yl)-5-(1-methyl-1H-pyrrol-2-yl)-4H-1,2,6-thiadiazin-4-one (12c).
Similar treatment of 3-chloro-5-(fur-2-yl)-4H-1,2,6-thiadiazin-4-one
(11b) (47 mg, 0.22 mmol) with 1-methyl-2-(tributylstannyl)pyrrole (87.1
μL, 0.264 mmol) gave the title compound 12c (57 mg, 100%) as yellow
needles. mp 87.5-90.5 °C (from cyclohexane), Rf 0.18 (hexane/DCM, 7:3);
(found: C, 55.5; H, 3.5; N, 16.1. C12H9N3O2S requires C, 55.6; H, 3.5; N,
16.2%); λmax(DCM)/nm 257 (log ε 2.88), 323 inf (2.65), 330 (2.67), 378
(3.05), 420 inf (2.91), 429 (2.93); νmax/cm-1 3165w, 3134w and 3113w (Ar
CH), 2949w, 1622s, 1611s (C=O), 1562w, 1524m, 1485s, 1466m, 1423m, 1412s,
1391m, 1368w, 1310s, 1279w, 1269w, 1246w, 1217w, 1180w, 1155w, 1146w,
1096w, 1082w, 1067s, 1047m, 1013w, 984w, 930w, 893w, 887w, 872w, 841w,
822w, 789w, 762m; δH(500 MHz; CDCl3) 7.83 (1H, dd, J 3.5, 0.5, furyl H),
7.72 (1H, dd, J 4.3, 1.8, pyrrolyl H), 7.66 (1H, dd, J 1.5, 0.5, furyl
H), 6.88 (1H, dd, J 4.5, 2.3, pyrrolyl H), 6.60 (1H, dd, J 3.5, 2.0,
furyl H), 6.25 (1H, dd, J 4.5, 2.5, pyrrolyl H), 3.96 (3H, s, NCH3);
δC(125 MHz; CDCl3) 161.2 (s), 152.5 (s), 149.0 (s), 148.1 (s), 145.7 (d),
131.0 (d), 126.4 (s), 120.4 (d), 118.7 (d), 112.6 (d), 108.5 (d), 38.6
(NCH3); m/z (EI) 259 (M+, 84%), 208 (7), 138 (49), 130 (6), 125 (100),
110 (10), 106 (40), 105 (19), 97 (11), 95 (9), 93 (12), 78 (8), 70 (12),
64 (10), 51 (5).
