$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM For catalytic analysis of the biomimetic materials, green synthetic
conditions were initially employed for the coupling of 4-iodobenzoic acid
and phenyltin trichloride to produce biphenyl carboxylic acid (BPCA),
which was used as a model system. 5 For this reaction, 0.500 mmol of the
aryl halide was codis-solved in solution with 0.600 mmol of phenyltin
trichloride using 8.00 mL of 2.25 M aqueous KOH. To this solution were
added varying amounts of the Pd materials (00.500 mol % of Pd), and the
reaction was stirred for 24.0 h. In this sense, the mol % of Pd refers to
the amount of Pd in solu- tion and not the concentration of
nanoparticles, which would be quite lower. Once complete, the reaction
was quenched with HCl, extracted using diethyl ether, and quantitated.
TABLE 2, entry 1, yield 100%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-catalyst, green chemistry-solvent, alternatively reaction
carried out using EtOH:H2O (3:1) solvent mixture gave 44.9% yield,
optimization study, optimized on stoichiometry of catalyst,
L-threonyl-L-seryl-L-asparaginyl-L-alanyl-L-valyl-L-histidyl-L-prolyl-L-threonyl-L-leucyl-L-arginyl-L-histidyl-L-leucine
surface functionalized palladium nanoparticle used as catalyst, Stille
cross coupling, reaction failed with 4-chlorobenzoic acid, alternatively
reaction using 4-bromobenzoic acid decreased yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Biomimetic Synthesis of Pd Nanocatalysts for the Stille Coupling Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Pacardo, Dennis B.; Sethi, Manish; Jones, Sharon E.; Naik, Rajesh R.;
Knecht, Marc R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM ACS Nano (2009), 3(5), 1288-1296

