$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: For catalytic analysis of the biomimetic
materials, green synthetic conditions were initially employed for the
coupling of 4-iodobenzoic acid and phenyltin trichloride to produce
biphenyl carboxylic acid (BPCA), which was used as a model system. 5 For
this reaction, 0.500 mmol of the aryl halide was codis-solved in solution
with 0.600 mmol of phenyltin trichloride using 8.00 mL of 2.25 M aqueous
KOH. To this solution were added varying amounts of the Pd materials
(00.500 mol % of Pd), and the reaction was stirred for 24.0 h. In this
sense, the mol % of Pd refers to the amount of Pd in solu- tion and not
the concentration of nanoparticles, which would be quite lower. Once
complete, the reaction was quenched with HCl, extracted using diethyl
ether, and quantitated. TABLE 2, entry 7, yield 100%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-catalyst, green chemistry-solvent,
L-threonyl-L-seryl-L-asparaginyl-L-alanyl-L-valyl-L-histidyl-L-prolyl-L-threonyl-L-leucyl-L-arginyl-L-histidyl-L-leucine
surface functionalized palladium nanoparticle used as catalyst, Stille
cross coupling, reaction failed with 4-chlorophenol, alternatively
reaction using 4-bromophenol decreased yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Biomimetic Synthesis of Pd Nanocatalysts for the Stille Coupling Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
