$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Stille Coupling with
Stannyl Thiophene and Stannyl Furan Reagents To a stirred solution of the
desired 5-bromo carbocyclic nucleoside (1.74 mmol) and aryl tin (8.72
mmol) in dioxane (50 mL) was added PdCl2(PPh3)2 (122 mg, 0.17 mmol) and
the temperature held at 90°C for 18 hours. The reaction mixture was then
evaporated to dryness and the residue purified by silica gel
chromatography eluting with hexanes:EtOAc (1:1).
1-[(2',3'-O-Isopropylidene)-4'-cyclopenten-1'-yl]-5-(thiophene-2-yl)-uracil
1-[(2',3'-O-Isopropylidene)-cyclopentan-1'-yl]-5-(thiophene-2-yl)uracil
Off-white solid (111 mg, 0.31 mmol, 99%). 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 1.32 (s, 3H),
1.51 (s, 3H), 1.95-2.05 (m, 2H), 2.21-2.25 (m, 1H), 2.39-2.41 (m, 1H),
4.44-4.49 (m, 1H), 4.83-4.85 (m, 1H), 4.88 (dd, 1H, J = 6.9, 14.8 Hz),
7.04 (dd, 1H, J = 9.2, 12.6), 7.29 (dd, 1H, J = 2.3, 12.6), 7.39 (dd, 1H,
J = 2.3, 9.1 Hz), 7.43 (s, 1H), 8.49 (s, 1H). 13C NMR (CD3OD): δ 12.6,
23.4, 26.0, 26.6, 27.9, 28.9, 31.0, 66.7, 80.9, 85.5, 109.7, 111.4,
123.6, 125.3, 126.2, 139.3. HRMS calculated for C16H18N2O4S [M]+
334.0987; found, 334.0979.
