$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure For Room-Temperature Stille
reactions of Aryl Bromides Using Ligand 4 (Procedure D). In a glove box,
the Schlenk tube equipped with a stir bar was charged with Pd2(dba)3
(11.2 mg, 0.012 mmol, 1.5 mol %), CsF (272 mg, 1.8 mmol), and ligand 4
(11 mg, 0.025 mmol, 3.0 mol %). The tube was fitted with a rubber septum
and removed out of the glove box. One mL of THF, aryl bromide (1.0 equiv)
and organotin reagent (1.1 equiv) were added successively using syringes.
The tube was sealed with a Teflon screwcap. The reaction mixture was
stirred at room temperature for the indicated time, and then diluted with
ether or acetone, filtered and concentrated in vacuo. The crude product
was purified by column chromatography on silica gel. 2,2’-Bithiophene
(Table 6, entry 11). Procedure D was followed using 2-bromothiophene (136
mg, 0.816 mmol) and (tributylstannyl)thiophene (0.27 mL, 0.898 mmol).
After the reaction was run at 50 °C for 30 h, the reaction mixture was
purified by column chromatography on silica gel (1% ethyl ether/pentane)
to afford 132 mg (98%) of the desired product as a white solid.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Stille cross-coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Highly active palladium catalysts supported by bulky proazaphosphatrane
ligands for Stille cross-coupling: Coupling of aryl and vinyl chlorides,
room temperature coupling of aryl bromides, coupling of aryl triflates,
and synthesis of sterically hindered biaryls
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
