$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):RGT(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 13400-13-0
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):CAT(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 51364-51-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):CAT(2):CAS_RN
$DATUM 130761-22-7
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 109-99-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure For Room-Temperature Stille reactions of Aryl Bromides
Using Ligand 4 (Procedure D). In a glove box, the Schlenk tube equipped
with a stir bar was charged with Pd2(dba)3 (11.2 mg, 0.012 mmol, 1.5 mol
%), CsF (272 mg, 1.8 mmol), and ligand 4 (11 mg, 0.025 mmol, 3.0 mol %).
The tube was fitted with a rubber septum and removed out of the glove
box. One mL of THF, aryl bromide (1.0 equiv) and organotin reagent (1.1
equiv) were added successively using syringes. The tube was sealed with a
Teflon screwcap. The reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for
the indicated time, and then diluted with ether or acetone, filtered and
concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel. 4-tert-Butylstyrene (Table 6, entry 1).
Procedure D was followed using 1-bromo-4-tert-butylbenzene (177 mg, 0.816
mmol) and vinyltributyltin (0.27ml, 0.898 mmol). After the reaction was
run for 10 h, the reaction mixture was purified by column chromatography
on silica gel (hexanes) to afford 129 mg (99%) of the desired product as
a colorless liquid.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Stille cross-coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Highly active palladium catalysts supported by bulky proazaphosphatrane
ligands for Stille cross-coupling: Coupling of aryl and vinyl chlorides,
room temperature coupling of aryl bromides, coupling of aryl triflates,
and synthesis of sterically hindered biaryls
