$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A 0.18-0.29 M DMF solution of bromopyrazines
(1) containing 2 mol% Pd[P(C6H5)3]4 was heated at 120 °C for 1.5-24 h
under nitrogen atmosphere. To the reaction mixture was added saturated
aqueous KF solution and stirred at room temperature for overnight. The
solution was diluted with CH2Cl2 and extracted with CH2Cl2 The organic
layer was concentrated to dryness after filtration and the crude mixture
was separated on a silica gel column to yield 2. Table 1, yield 99%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 5- and 3,5-substituted 2-aminopyrazines by Pd mediated
Stille coupling
