$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Method B: A mixture of 3,5-dibromo-1-methyl-1H-1,2,4-triazole (1) (200
mg, 0.83 mmol), stannyl derivative (2) (2.16 mmol), PdCl2(PPh3)2 (24 mg,
0.033 mmol) and LiCl (106 mg, 2.49 mmol) was irradiated under Argon in a
focused microwave reactor reactor DiscoverTM (CEM) at 130 °C during the
appropiate time. The crude products 5a-c were purified by flash
chromatography on silica gel using a mixture of hexane:ethyl acetate as
the eluent. 1-methyl-3,5-di(thiophen-2-yl)-1H-1,2,4-triazole 5a. Method
B. Tributyl(thiophen-2-yl)stannane 2a (806 mg, 2.16 mmol) and LiCl were
used. The crude was purified with a mixture of hexane:ethyl acetate (6:1)
as the eluent, 5a (202mg, 98%) was obtained. Mp 107-108 °C; 1H NMR
(CDCl3): δ = 7.71 (dd, J = 3.7, 1.1 Hz, 1 H, H-3'), 7,54 (dd, J = 3.7,
1.1 Hz, 1 H, H-3''), 7.53 (dd, J = 5.1, 1.1 Hz, 1 H, H-5''), 7.34 (dd, J
= 4.8, 1.1 Hz, 1 H, H-5'), 7.18 (dd, J = 5.1, 3.7 Hz, 1 H, H-4''), 7.10
(dd, J = 5.1, 3.7 Hz, 1 H, H-4'), 4.07 (s, 3 H, CH3); 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ
= 157.3, 150.0, 133.5, 128.9, 128.7, 128.6, 127.9, 127.6, 126.3, 126.2,
37.1 (CH3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Stille reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Microwave-assisted Stille reactions as a powerful tool for building
polyheteroaryl systems bearing a (1H)-1,2,4-triazole moiety
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
