$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Stille Coupling An
oven-dried Wheaton screw cap vial was charged with 1A (2 mol%) and
Pd(OAc)2 or Pd(OCOCF3)2 (2 mol%), CsF (2 mmol) and 2 mL anhyd dioxane.
After ca 10 min (the solution turned blackish red) aryl bromide (1 mmol)
was added and after an additional 10 min organostannane (1 mmol) was
added. The tube was then briefly flushed with argon, tightly capped then
heated at 100 °C. After all starting material had been consumed, as
judged by TLC, the reaction mixture was quenched by diluting with Et2O,
washed with two portions of H2O followed by brine, dried over Na2SO4,
filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude product was
purified by flash chromatography on silica gel. Table 2, entry 12, yield
98%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Stille cross-coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
