$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthetic Procedures and Characterization. Synthesis of
2-(5-(9,9-Bis(2-(2-ethoxyethoxy)ethyl)-7-nitro-9Hfluoren-
2-yl)thiophen-2-yl)benzothiazole (3). In a 10 mL vessel, under nitrogen,
9,9-bis(2-(2-ethoxyethoxy)ethyl)-2- iodo-7-nitro-9H-fluorene (1; 200 mg,
0.335 mmol), 2-(5- (tributylstannyl)thiophen-2-yl)benzothiazole (2; 207
mg, 0.408 mmol), and Pd(PPh3)2Cl2 (6 mg, 0.008 mmol) were dissolved in
toluene (2 mL). The mixture was heated in the microwave for 25 min, at
130 °C, 150 psi, and 150 W, filtered through a Celite plug, and purified
by column chromatography using as a solvent a mixture of hexane/ethyl
acetate (2:1). 216 mg (98%) of a light orange solid. mp 75.7−76.5 °C. 1H
NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.26−8.34 (m, 2H, Ph-H), 8.06 (d, J = 8.06 Hz, 1H,
Ph-H), 7.89 (d, J = 8.06 Hz, 1H, Ph-H), 7.73−7.84 (m, 4H, Ph-H), 7.69 (d,
J = 3.93 Hz, 1H, Thy-H), 7.49−7.52 (m, 1H, Ph-H), 7.48 (d, J = 3.93 Hz,
1H, Thy-H), 7.38−7.42 (m, 1H, Ph-H), 3.34−3.40 (m, 4H, CH2), 3.27−3.31
(m, 4H, CH2), 3.15−3.22 (m, 4H, CH2), 2.79−2.93 (m, 4H, CH2), 2.45−2.56
(m, 4H, CH2), 1.10 (t, J = 6.98 Hz, 6H, CH3). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ
161.1, 153.9, 152.1, 151.2, 147.7, 147.5, 146.3, 138.6, 137.0, 135.0,
134.8, 129.7, 126.8, 126.0, 125.6, 124.8, 123.9, 123.2, 122.2, 121.7,
121.0, 120.2, 119.3, 70.4, 69.8, 67.1, 66.8, 52.5, 39.6, 15.2. MS (APCI)
m/z calcd [M + H]+ 659.2244, found 659.2256.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM high pressure, microwave irradiation (150 W), thermal, Sonogashira
coupling reaction
