$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure F (no glove box). Pd2(dba)3, CsF,
the aryl bromide, NMP, a solution of P(t-Bu)3 in NMP, and the organotin
reagent were added in turn to a 4-mL vial equipped with a stir bar. The
vial was capped with a rubber septum under an argon atmosphere and
allowed to stir at room temperature for the indicated amount of time. The
workup was the same as that for Procedure C.
1-(1-Ethoxyvinyl)-2,4-dimethoxybenzene. Colorless liquid. Yield: 202 mg
(97%). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.43-7.46 (m,1H), 6.47-6.50 (m,2H),
4.60 (d,J= 1.8 Hz, 1H), 4.36 (d,J= 1.8 Hz, 1H), 3.89 (q, J= 7.0 Hz, 2H),
3.84 (s, 3H), 3.82 (s, 3H), 1.39 (t, J= 7.0 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR (75MHz,
CDCl3): 160.9, 158.3, 157.6, 130.3, 119.6, 104.3, 99.1, 86.0, 63.2, 55.8,
55.6, 14.8. IR (neat, cm-1): 2974, 2936, 2837, 1723, 1608, 1505, 1463,
1440, 1416, 1365, 1257, 1210, 1162, 1099, 1034, 975, 941, 925, 834, 802,
770. HRMS (EI, m/z) calcd. For C12H16O3 (M+):208.1099. Found: 218.1103.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Pd/P(t-Bu)3: A Mild and General Catalyst for Stille Reactions of Aryl
Chlorides and Aryl Bromides
