$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure D (no glove box). Pd2(dba)3, the
aryl bromide, a solution of p(t-Bu)3 in toluene), toluene, and the
organotin reagent were added in turn to a 4-mL vial equipped with a stir
bar. The vial was capped with a rubber septum under an argon atmosphere
and allowed to stir at room temperature for the indicated amount of time.
The workup was the same as that for Procedure C.
1-Methyl-2-phenylethynylbenzene. colorless liquid.Yield: 184 mg (95%). 1H
NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.57-7.63 (m, 3H), 7.38-7.45 (m, 3H), 7.20-7.30
(m, 3H), 2.60 (s, 3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Pd/P(t-Bu)3: A Mild and General Catalyst for Stille Reactions of Aryl
Chlorides and Aryl Bromides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
