$DATUM Ligand 1b: 2-bromopyridine (1.48 g, 0.89 mL, 9.4 mmol),
2-methyl-5-(tributylstannyl)thiophene (4.0 g, 10.3 mmol), Pd(PPh3)4 (0.54
g, 0.47 mmol) and CsF (3.12 g, 20.6 mmol) were weighed into a Schlenk
tube and 60 mL of dioxane was added. The reaction mixture was sparged for
15 minutes with argon. The reaction mixture was heated at 100 °C for 36
hours. The reaction mixture was cooled down and was passed through a
silica gel plug to remove the solids. The silica plug was eluted with 250
mL of ethyl acetate. The combined organic fractions were evaporated to
yield an oily residue, which was chromatographed on silica gel with
dichloromethane/hexane (2:1 v/v) as the eluent to yield 1.59 g (97%) of
1b as a white solid. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.53 (d, 1H), 7.64 (t,
1H), 7.58 (d, 1H), 7.38 (d, 1H), 7.10 (t, 1H), 6.76 (d, 1H), 2.53 (s,
3H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 153.0, 149.6, 142.7, 137.7, 126.5, 124.8,
122.6, 118.5, 15.9. HRMS calcd. for C10H10NS (M+H)+, 176.0529; found,
176.0530. mp = 77-78 °C.
