$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method D: A mixture of
1-phenyl-4-(tributylstannyl)-1H-1,2,3-triazole (100 mg, 0.23 mmol.),
halogenated derivative (12) (0.27 mmol), PdCl2(PPh3)2 (3 mg, 0.004 mmol)
and LiCl (29.3 mg, 0.69 mmol) was irradiated at the temperature and
during the appropriate time under Argon in a focused microwave reactor
DiscoverTM (CEM). The crude products 13a-g were purified by flash
chromatography on silica gel using a mixture of hexane:ethyl acetate as
the eluent. 4-(3-bromophenyl)-1-phenyl-1H-1,2,3-triazole 13c. Method D.
1,3-dibromobenzene 12c (64.7 mg, 0.27 mmol) were used. The crude was
purified with a mixture of hexane:ethyl acetate (9:1) as the eluent, 13c
(66 mg, 96%) was obtained as a yellow oil. 1H-NMR (CDCl3) δ 8.2 (s, 1H),
8.0 (m, 1H), 7.8-7.7 (m, 3H), 7.6-7.5 (m, 4H), 7.3 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 1H,
p-H Ph). 13C-NMR (CDCl3) δ 147.0, 136.9, 132.3, 131.3, 130.5, 129.8,
128.9, 128.8, 124.4, 123.0, 120.6, 117.9.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Stille reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Microwave-assisted Stille reactions as a powerful tool for building
polyheteroaryl systems bearing a (1H)-1,2,4-triazole moiety
