$DATUM 14592-56-4
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 18. Representative protocol for the Stille-coupling on the solid phase:
To resin 5 (0.5 g, 0.256 mmol) were added freshly distilled dioxane (5.1
ml), 2-(tributylstannyl)furan (297 mg, 0.769 mmol) and Ph3As (32 mg,
0.103 mmol) and the resulting suspension was degassed with argon for 20
min. Pd2(dba)3 (23.5 mg, 0.026 mmol) was added at once and the reaction
was shaken at 50°C for 24h. The solid phase was filtered and washed with
5 ml each of dioxane (6 x), CH2Cl2 (6 x), MeOH (3 x), dioxane (3 x) and
Et2O (3 x). The resin was dried under vacuum and suspended in dioxane
(8.3 ml). Sodium (35 mg, 1.53 mmol) was dissolved in MeOH (2.1 ml) and
the resulting solution of NaOMe was added. The reaction mixture was
shaken for 24h at RT. The resin was filtered off and further extracted
with 5 ml each of dioxane (4 x), H2O (6 x), phosphate buffer, pH=7 (3 x),
dioxane (3 x), EtOH:H2O (1:1, 3 x), EtOH (3 x), ether (3 x). The combined
liquid phases were concentrated and the resulting solid was extracted
with CH2Cl2. After filtration through celite and concentration crude
product (entry 2, Table 4) was obtained which was shown to be 98% pure by
1H-NMR (400 MHz). Table 4, entry 2, yield 43.8 mg, 98%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM RESIN USED
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Palladium-mediated C-C and C-S bond formation on solid support. A scope
and limitations study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wendeborn, Sebastian; Berteina, Sabine; Brill, Wolfgang K.-D.; De
Mesmaeker, Alain
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (1998), (6), 671-675

