$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Stille Reaction with Compounds 5; General Procedure (Method A) To a
stirred mixture of 5 (0.33 mmol), freshly prepared Pd(PPh3)4 (30 mg, 0.03
mmol, 0.08 equiv) and LiCl (35 mg, 0.82 mmol, 2.5 equiv) in anhyd DMF (3
mL) was added tributyl(1-ethoxyvinyl)tin (160 mL, 0.49 mmol, 1.5 equiv).
The mixture was stirred at 90 °C for 12 h and then the solvent was
evaporated in vacuo. The crude residue was purified by flash
chromatography (eluent indicated below) to give 6a-c.
8-Acetyl-4-(N-methyl-N-phenylamino)pyrazolo[1,5-a]-1,3,5- triazine (6a)
Chromatography eluent: PE, then EtOAc-PE (1:9, then 2:8); yield: 96%;
solid. Mp 120-121 °C (MeOH). IR (KBr): 1655, 1590, 1545 cm-1. 1H NMR (300
MHz, CDCl3): δ = 2.69 (s, 3 H, CH3), 3.84 (s, 3 H, CH3), 7.18-7.21 (m, 2
H, ArH), 7.38-7.43 (m, 3 H, ArH), 8.20 (s, 1 H, H-7), 8.38 (s, 1 H, H-2).
13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 29.3 (CH3), 42.8 (CH3), 111.3 (C), 126.3 (2
CH), 128.0 (CH), 129.5 (2 CH), 144.3 (C), 145.8 (CH), 150.3 (C), 151.6
(C), 155.5 (CH), 192.3 (C=O). MS (ESI): m/z = 268 (M + H)+. Anal. Calcd
for C14H13N5O: C, 62.91; H, 4.90; N, 26.20. Found: C, 62.73; H, 4.87; N,
26.03.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Stille coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 8-substituted pyrazolo[1,5-a]-1,3,5-triazine derivatives by
palladium-catalyzed cross-coupling reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Popowycz, Florence; Bernard, Philippe; Raboisson, Pierre; Joseph, Benoit
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2007), (3), 367-374

