$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Acylation of Bromopyrazines, 1,2-Bromopyridine
(6) and Bromobenzenes; General Procedure. A mixture of the corresponding
hetaryl or aryl bromides (0.50 mmol), PdCl2(Ph3P)2 (18 mg, 0.026 mmol, 5
mol%) and 95% CuI (15 mg, 0.075 mmol, 15 mol%) in anhyd MeCN (4.0 mL) was
placed under argon, and tributyl(1-ethoxyvinyl)tin (2;12 0.54 g, 1.5
mmol) or tributyl(1-ethoxyprop-1-enyl)tin (4;1 0.56 g, 1.5 mmol) was
introduced by a syringe. After heating for the time given in Tables 1-3,
1.5 M aq HCl (20 mL) was added to quench the reaction. The solution was
refluxed for 1 h, neutralized with NaHCO3 and extracted with EtOAc (3 15
mL). The combined extracts were dried (MgSO4) and concentrated under
reduced pressure. To the residue was added sat. KF-MeOH13 (3 mL), and the
mixture was filtered. After removal of the solvent, the residue was
chromatographed on Silica Gel 60 (hexane-EtOAc, 4:1-15:1) to provide the
acyl compounds. 5,6-Diphenyl-2-propionylpyrazine (5d). Colorless needles,
yield 96%. Mp 105-106°C (EtOH). IR (KBr): ν = 1698 (C=O), 1356, 1267,
1168, 1102, 966, 771, 696 cm-1. 1H NMR (400 MHz): δ = 1.26 (t, 3H, J =
7.2 Hz), 3.31 (q, 2H, J = 7.2 Hz), 7.30-7.37 (m, 6H), 7.49-7.52 (m, 4H),
9.20 (s, 1H). 13C NMR (100.6 MHz): δ = 7.8, 31.4, 128.2, 128.3, 128.4,
129.0, 129.3, 129.6, 129.7, 138.0, 140.3, 144.6, 151.1, 155.3, 202.1. MS:
m/z (%) = 289 (MH+, 100). Anal. Calcd for C19H16N2O: C, 79.14; H, 5.59;
N, 9.72. Found: C, 79.13; H, 5.86; N, 9.93.
