$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure A. In a dry box, Pd2dba3 (1.5 mol%),
and P(furyl)3 (3.5 mol %), and LiCl (for triflates) were added to the
reaction vessel equipped with a stir bar, which was capped with a septum
and removed from the dry box. Diene 1 and the halide in NMP were added by
syringe. The flask was wrapped with foil and stirred at the indicated
temperature under argon until TLC indicated starting halide had been
consumed. The reaction mixture was diluted with ether and poured into
saturated aqueous NH4Cl. The aqueous layer was extracted with ether (3x)
and the combined organic extracts were dried (MgSO4), and evaporated in
vacuo. The crude product was purified by flash chromatography
(Florisil®).
4,4,5,5-Tetramethyl-2-((1E,3E)-4-(2,6-dimethylphenyl)buta-1,3-dienyl)-1,3,2-dioxaborolane
(14) (Table 1, entry 6). Procedure A was followed, using 2-iodo-m-xylene
(54.0 mg, 0.234 mmol), 1 (121 mg, 0.257 mmol), Pd2dba3 (3.1 mg. 4.0
μmol), P(furyl)3 (2.1 mg, 9.0 μmol), and NMP (1.5 mL). After 24 h at 50
°C, workup and column chromatography (0-10% EtOAc/hexane) afforded 14
(64.0 mg, 96%) as a light yellow oil: light yellow oil 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.25 (dd, 1H, J = 10.4, 17.6 Hz), 7.07 (m, 3H), 6.81 (d, 1H, J =
16.0 Hz). 6.42 (dd, 1H, J = 10.4, 16.0 Hz), 5.65 (d, 1H, J = 17.6 Hz) 2.4
(s, 6H), 1.32 (s, 12H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 150.2, 136.2, 136.1,
136.1, 134.7, 128.0, 127.0, 83.3, 24.8, 21.1; IR (KBr) ν max 2977, 2927,
2854, 1629, 1603, 1466, 1356, 1323, 1260, 1145, 1010, 970, 850, 769 cm–1;
HRMS (ESI) m/z 284.1946 (calcd for C18H25BO2Na: 284.1942).
